ent":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_farmers_markets\"\n7944\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914625797},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have:\n- Total farmers markets: 7,944\n- US Population 2025: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to create a derived metric that calculates the ratio: farmers_markets per 100,000 residents.\n\nThe calculation should be: (7944 / 341784857) * 100000\n\nLet me create a build script that reads both sources, gets these aggregated values, and calculates the per-100k metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a build script that calculates the farmers markets per 100,000 residents by joining the aggregates from both sources."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01CEdgXyrURiyFiXDSas5qVp","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census population data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets to get total\ntotals = fact.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population estimate for 2025\ndenom = (ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\")\n            .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and calculate per 100,000 residents\nexpr = (\n    totals.join(denom, totals.k == denom.k)\n      .mutate(farmers_markets_per_100k=totals.total_farmers_markets / denom.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":701,"cacheRead":17749,"cacheWrite":221,"totalTokens":18683,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0035050000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0017749000000000003,"cacheWrite":0.00027625,"total":0.005568150000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":109},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914625798,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77Z1HNuZfESdCeJ6VSk","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01CEdgXyrURiyFiXDSas5qVp","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1305 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914633186},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BKktaWXQvn2FzXuFkPRFFZ","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-22-17gko4hh && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp3.txt 2>&1 && cat /tmp/bp3.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":146,"cacheRead":17970,"cacheWrite":745,"totalTokens":18874,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0007300000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0017970000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00093125,"total":0.0034712500000000004},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":12},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914633188,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77ZXnBUh8MBf4uP13WQ","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BKktaWXQvn2FzXuFkPRFFZ","toolName":"bash","